\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Federated learning for CSI-based HAR. Each home senses activities through Wi-Fi CSI (house $+$ access point $+$ person) but observes only a subset of activity classes. \textbf  {(A)}~Non-cooperative clients train only on their own data, so each recognises just its local classes (green chips). \textbf  {(B)}~Federated distillation lets every client recognise \emph  {activities it never observed locally} by absorbing peer knowledge through the server, while raw data stays private.}}{1}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fedhar}{{1}{1}{}{figure.1}{}}
